worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_19.js"
  ceiling 1250
  rationale "Part of the mechanically split browser mirror of the Rust solver: issue #658 divided one oversized worker file by line count, so this shard has no subject of its own. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into js/wasm-worker. Ceiling 1314 (2026-10-07, PR #1188): tryProjectLookup leaves an install guide being converted to installation_conversion, which Rust asks before its repository lookup. Ceiling moved to 1316 for issue #918 (2026-10-08): the response-language follow-up reads its terse word limit from the policy block of data/seed/handler-rules.lino and declines the same inconclusive replay intents as the native engine (concept_lookup_unresolved). Ceiling moved 1316 to 1318: tryResponseLanguageFollowup declines a directive that forbids the language it names (R384 follow-up, 2026-10-08), as try_response_language_followup does natively. Lowered to 1309 for issue #918 (2026-10-08): the four-language web search text table became seeded web_search_* responses read by webSearchTexts. Lowered to 1250 for issue #1175 R3 (last five rows, 2026-10-08): tryGithubRepositoryTraffic runs the github_repository_traffic rules, which name the repository the prompt names, instead of a four-role recognizer that always named the agent-info repository."
